<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prayagraj</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Allahabad, Prayag</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prayagraj, called Allahabad from the time of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a> until 2018, is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, at the confluence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a>, a sacred bathing place for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindus</a>. It hosts the Kumbh Mela, one of the largest religious gatherings in the world. Its fort holds the Ashokan pillar bearing the Allahabad inscription of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samudragupta">Samudragupta</a>, and it was a centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a> movement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prayagraj.jpg" alt="Prayagraj" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dananuj · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Allahabad_Montage_II_Dec_2014.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
